# Without this file none of the components below is a type for a component
# loaded BY URL (PluginNode / PluginBarWidget `source:`): under Quickshell's
# `qs:` scheme Qt adds no implicit import for the containing directory, so a
# bare sibling reference fails with "X is not a type" - exactly how the media
# widget's tree shipped broken. The bar's own DiscordVoicePlugin reaches this
# package through a directory import, which happens to register types without
# a qmldir - so the popup worked while Widget.qml and BarWidget.qml were
# latent failures waiting for someone to place them. One qmldir serves every
# load path. See docs/PLUGINS.md, "Multi-file packages".
# Every component here, not only the ones referenced bare: a qmldir DISABLES
# the directory-import auto-listing, so the moment this file exists, every
# `DiscordPackage.X` consumer sees only what is listed. The registration lint
# caught exactly that half-listing before it shipped.
module DiscordVoiceWidget
Widget Widget.qml
BarWidget BarWidget.qml
DiscordGlyph DiscordGlyph.qml
DiscordVoicePopup DiscordVoicePopup.qml
ParticipantAvatar ParticipantAvatar.qml
TaskbarGlyph TaskbarGlyph.qml
